## Cost summary

| Component | Provider | Cost |
|---|---|---|
| Satellite imagery | Copernicus (Sentinel-2) | $0 — free by EU policy |
| Scene discovery | STAC API (Element84 / Microsoft / CDSE) | $0 — public API |
| Computation | GitHub Actions | $0 — free for public repos (uses ~18 of 2,000 free min/month) |
| Data storage | Git repository | $0 — the CSV grows at roughly 500 KB/year |
| Web hosting | GitHub Pages | $0 — free for public repos |
| Map tiles | OpenStreetMap | $0 — free and open |
| Charts | Chart.js (CDN) | $0 — open source |
| Domain (optional) | Any registrar | ~$10/year (optional — works fine on github.io) |
| Monitoring | The dashboard itself | $0 — stale dates are self-evident |
| **Total** | | **$0/month** |

---

## Risks and mitigations

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|
| GitHub changes Actions free tier | Low | High | Migrate workflow to any CI with cron support (GitLab CI, Codeberg). The script is platform-agnostic. |
| Primary STAC API goes offline | Medium | Low | Automatic fallback to two alternative STAC endpoints serving the same data. |
| Sentinel-2 mission ends | Very low | High | ESA's Copernicus program has a continuity mandate. Sentinel-2 Next Gen is already planned. Landsat provides a degraded but functional backup. |
| NDWI threshold drift over time | Low | Medium | Surface area estimates may diverge from reality if dam morphology changes (new construction, major silting). Periodic recalibration (once every few years) is advisable but not critical — relative trends remain valid. |
| Extended cloud cover | Medium | Low | Tunisia is predominantly sunny. A missed reading is filled by the next clear pass. Gaps are visible on the dashboard and self-correcting. |
| GitHub disables the workflow | Low | Medium | The system's own commits (pushing updated data) count as repository activity, preventing the 60-day inactivity cutoff. |
| Data is misused or misinterpreted | Medium | Medium | Clear disclaimers on the dashboard: this is satellite-derived surface extent, not volumetric measurement. Surface area is a proxy for volume, not a replacement for bathymetric survey. |
| The original developer disappears | Certain | None | This is the design goal. MIT license, public repository, simple architecture. Anyone can fork and it keeps running. |

---

## What this is not

This system does not replace professional hydrological monitoring. It does not measure reservoir volume (which requires bathymetric data). It does not detect underground pipe leaks. It does not provide real-time flood warnings. It does not run weather models.

What it does is take free satellite data that flies over Tunisia every 5 days, compute a simple water index, publish the result on a public website, and accumulate a historical record. It does this forever, for free, without anyone needing to be involved.

The value is not in the sophistication of the analysis. The value is in the fact that it runs.
